From 685872ec19652befba6d3647c92be79b14713efe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 17:33:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] gweb: Don't close socket twice when channel is unref'd

When connect() fails at once (for example ENETUNREACH while the bearer
has no route), connect_session_transport() closed the socket, and
free_session() closed it again when it dropped the channel, which has
close-on-unref set. Anything that reused the descriptor in between,
such as the file a request is being stored in, lost it.

Backported from ConnMan commit c303dc3c2d92 ("gweb: Don't close socket
twice when channel is unref'd") by Peter Meerwald
<p.meerwald@bct-electronic.com>. Upstream message:

  since g_io_channel_set_close_on_unref() is called on the channel, no
  need to close socket manually beforehand, this fixes

  (connmand:14087): GLib-WARNING **: Invalid file descriptor.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Backport [https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/network/connman/connman.git/commit/?id=c303dc3c2d92efc44668a06d0da84ce934a81f43]
---
 gweb/gweb.c | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/gweb/gweb.c b/gweb/gweb.c
index 327f48b..5597089 100644
--- a/gweb/gweb.c
+++ b/gweb/gweb.c
@@ -1065,7 +1065,6 @@ static int connect_session_transport(struct web_session *session)
 			session->addr->ai_addrlen) < 0) {
 		if (errno != EINPROGRESS) {
 			debug(session->web, "connect() %s", strerror(errno));
-			close(sk);
 			return -EIO;
 		}
 	}
